'''''Monarch: Legacy of Monsters''''' is an American [[Monster movie|monster]] television series created by [[Chris Black (screenwriter)|Chris Black]] and [[Matt Fraction]] and produced by [[Legendary Entertainment|Legendary Television]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=babrams |date=January 16, 2024 |title=''Monarch: Legacy of Monsters'' Creators Matt Fraction and Chris Black on What Made Season One Roar |url=https://www.motionpictures.org/2024/01/monarch-legacy-of-monsters-creators-matt-fraction-and-chris-black-on-what-made-season-one-roar/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240116014948/https://www.motionpictures.org/2024/01/monarch-legacy-of-monsters-creators-matt-fraction-and-chris-black-on-what-made-season-one-roar/ |archive-date=January 16, 2024 |access-date=January 16, 2024 |publisher=[[Motion Picture Association]] |language=en-US}}</ref> Based on [[Godzilla]] by [[Toho|Toho Co., Ltd]], it is the sixth installment and second television series in the [[Monsterverse]] franchise. Following the events of ''[[Godzilla (2014 film)|Godzilla]]'' (2014), the series follows members of the Monarch organization as they encounter [[Godzilla (Monsterverse)|Godzilla]] and other monsters called Titans, across a half century.

The series stars [[Anna Sawai]], [[Kiersey Clemons]], Ren Watabe, [[Mari Yamamoto]], [[Anders Holm]], [[Joe Tippett]] and [[Elisa Lasowski]], alongside son-father duo [[Wyatt Russell|Wyatt]] and [[Kurt Russell]] in the shared role of Lee Shaw. ''Monarch: Legacy of Monsters'' premiered on [[Apple TV+]] on November 17, 2023, to positive reviews. In April 2024, the series was renewed for a second season, which premiered on February 27, 2026.<ref name="S2Premiere"/>

==Premise==
In 2015, one year after the re-emergence of [[Godzilla (Monsterverse)|Godzilla]],{{Efn|name=Godzilla2014}} half-siblings Cate and Kentaro Randa investigate their missing father Hiroshi's connection to Monarch, the covert organization monitoring giant monsters known as [[Kaiju|Titans]] or [[MUTO]]s ("Massive Unidentified Terrestrial Organisms"). Two generations earlier, Bill Randa and Keiko Miura are scientists involved with the early development of Monarch. Former Army officer Lee Shaw becomes a close ally to the Randa family across both time periods.

==Cast and characters==
===Main===
* [[Anna Sawai]] as Cate Randa: A San Francisco schoolteacher coping with [[Post-traumatic stress disorder|PTSD]] whose search for her missing father leads her to uncover his involvement with Monarch<ref name="June2022Casting" />
* [[Kiersey Clemons]] as May Olowe-Hewitt: A former employee of Applied Experimental Technologies (later Apex Cybernetics{{Efn|name=GodzillaVsKong|As depicted in ''[[Godzilla vs. Kong]]'' (2021)}}) who fled to Japan under an alias after discovering that her company was using her code for nefarious purposes. Her real name is later revealed as Corah Mateo.<ref name="June2022Casting" />
* Ren Watabe as Kentaro Randa: An artist and Cate's half-brother who joins her on a journey to find their mysterious father<ref name="June2022Casting" />
* [[Mari Yamamoto]] as Keiko Miura: A scientist who investigates monsters with Lee Shaw and Bill Randa in the 1950s<ref name="Yamamoto" />
* [[Anders Holm]] as Bill Randa: A [[cryptozoology|cryptozoologist]] who becomes a leading researcher for Monarch<ref name="Holm" />
** [[John Goodman]] as an older Bill Randa (guest season 1), reprising his role from ''[[Kong: Skull Island]]'' (2017)<ref name="Goodman" />
* [[Joe Tippett]] as Tim: An overzealous Monarch office worker who goes into the field to track down the organization's lost documents<ref name="June2022Casting" />
* [[Wyatt Russell]] and [[Kurt Russell]] as Lee Shaw: A former U.S. Army colonel who joins Keiko and Bill in their investigations of monsters and subsequently becomes involved with Monarch. Kurt portrays the older version of Shaw, encountered by Cate and Kentaro, while Wyatt plays the younger version, responsible for founding Monarch.<ref name="RussellsCast" /><ref name="FirstLookAugust2023" />
* [[Elisa Lasowski]] as Michelle Duvall (season 1): The sister of the late Sandra Brody{{Efn|As depicted in ''[[Godzilla (2014 film)|Godzilla]]'' (2014)|name=Godzilla2014}} and a skilled Monarch operative partnered with Tim<ref name="June2022Casting" />

