==Production==
===Development===
Following the success of ''[[Godzilla vs. Kong]]'', discussions commenced on ways that the ''MonsterVerse'' could be expanded beyond feature films. [[Legendary Entertainment|Legendary]] proposed a live-action series, and among the potential investors, Apple TV+ expressed immediate interest, negotiated a deal, and [[Green-light|green-lit]] the series in January 2022. It is a joint venture between [[Legendary Entertainment#Legendary Television and Digital Media|Legendary Television]], Safehouse Pictures, and [[Toho]], although [[Warner Bros.]] still owns the rights for the ''[[MonsterVerse]]'' franchise alongside [[Legendary Entertainment|Legendary]]. [[Chris Black (screenwriter)|Chris Black]] and [[Matt Fraction]] are creators with Black as showrunner.<ref name="TitansTV_Collider"/><ref name="TitansTV_Deadline"/> In May, [[Matt Shakman]] was hired to direct the first two episodes in addition to executive producing.<ref name="Shakman"/> In addition to Black and [[Matt Fraction]], writers include [[Andrew Colville (writer)|Andrew Colville]], Milla Bell-Hart, Amanda Overton, [[Karl Taro Greenfeld]], [[Mariko Tamaki]], and Al Letson.<ref name="WGA"/>

On April 11, 2024, Apple TV+ renewed the series for a second season, with several spinoffs in development.<ref name="S2Renewal"/> In October 2026, it was reported that a third season was in development, with Legendary Television seeking a new showrunner and new writers to join the series.<ref name="S3Development"/>

===Casting===
In June 2022, [[Anna Sawai]], Ren Watabe, [[Kiersey Clemons]], [[Joe Tippett]], and [[Elisa Lasowski]] were cast.<ref name="June2022Casting" /> In July, [[Kurt Russell]] and [[Wyatt Russell]] were cast,<ref name="RussellsCast" /> and [[Mari Yamamoto]] joined in August.<ref name="Yamamoto" /> In September, [[Anders Holm]] was cast and revealed the title.<ref name="Holm"/> In September 2023, the teaser trailer revealed [[John Goodman]] to reprise his role from ''[[Kong: Skull Island]]'' (2017) as William "Bill" Randa.<ref name="Goodman"/>

===Filming===
In July 2022, it was revealed that [[principal photography]] had commenced in [[Vancouver]], [[British Columbia]], [[Canada]].<ref name="PrincipalPhotography" /> Two weeks of filming occurred in Japan in August.<ref name="JapanFilming"/>

Filming for the second season was underway by July 31, 2024,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Northrup |first=Ryan |date=July 31, 2024 |title=Monarch: Legacy Of Monsters Season 2 Gets Major Filming Update With BTS Photo From Anna Sawai |url=https://screenrant.com/monarch-legacy-of-monsters-season-2-filming-update-anna-sawai-image/ |access-date=July 31, 2024 |website=[[Screen Rant]]}}</ref> and wrapped by February 20, 2025.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Kimathi |first1=Denis |date=February 20, 2025 |title='Monarch' Season 2 Gets a Titan-Sized Filming Update |url=https://collider.com/monarch-legacy-of-monsters-season-2-wraps-filming/ |access-date=February 24, 2025 |website=[[Valnet#Collider|Collider]]}}</ref>

===Music===
In October 2023, [[Leopold Ross]] was confirmed as score composer.<ref name="Score" /> The soundtrack was released online by [[Milan Records]] on November 17, 2023, with the [[main titles]] track released on November 3 as a [[Single (music)|single]].<ref name="Soundtrack" /> The soundtrack for the second season was released online by Milan Records on February 27, 2026.<ref name="Season2Soundtrack" />

